# ghost buddy — build prompt
<!--⁠‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌‌⁠ uberdesigner prompt format v1 · ghost-buddy · v1.0.0 -->

## Goal
You're building a single full-window UI piece: a small glowing **glass ghost** drawn on a canvas in the middle of a
near-black page, which reacts to the cursor. It's a rounded-dome ghost with a four-scallop wavy hem, filled with a deep
violet glass gradient lit from inside (blue top left, magenta bottom right, a teal glint), a soft cyan / magenta /
violet chromatic aura behind it, RGB-split edge lines, faint scanlines, an inset glowing rim, a white specular arc on
the dome and two glowing white eyes. Behind it: a violet glow that follows the ghost, a barely visible pattern of
interlocking circles and 26 drifting dust motes. **Every expression is one eye shape that morphs smoothly into the
next.** The eyes track the cursor while the ghost leans and drifts toward it and its hem trails behind; hovering it
melts the eyes into happy arches (^ ^) and turns up the glow; clicking it squashes it like jelly with > < eyes,
sparkles and a ripple ring; clicking elsewhere makes it flinch (a small ripple there) and look; a fast cursor flick
startles it (round dot eyes, a hop and an RGB glitch); after 5 seconds without moving it falls asleep with sleepy eyes
and a floating "z"; with the cursor out of the window it looks around on its own. On phones the finger takes the
cursor's place (tap, hold, drag, swipe). The original is a single-file Canvas 2D concept; this build matches it frame
for frame at 60 fps and adds the touch mapping, fixes for the wake-up hop, slow frames and a zero-size start, and
reduced motion. Match everything below exactly:
look, motion and timing. There are no images and no fonts to load.

## Stack and setup
- Vite + React 19 + TypeScript (strict). Plain CSS: a tokens file, a global file and one CSS Module. **No other
  libraries**: the ghost is plain Canvas 2D in typed modules, driven by one `requestAnimationFrame` loop.
- Create and run:
  ```bash
  npm create vite@latest ghost-buddy -- --template react-ts --no-interactive
  cd ghost-buddy
  npm install
  npm run dev
