## Motion
The code below is the source of truth; this is what it does. Times in seconds, "rate r" means an exponential ease
`x += (target − x)(1 − e^(−r·dt))`.

| Behaviour | Trigger | What moves | Values |
|---|---|---|---|
| Loop | every animation frame | everything | `dt = clamp((now − last) / 1000, 0.001, 0.033)`, then `update`, then `draw` |
| Follow | cursor in the window | body drifts toward the cursor, bobs | target = centre + (clamp(dx·0.06, ±0.16U), clamp(dy·0.04, ±0.1U)) + bob sin(1.5t)·0.035U; spring k 28, damping 7.5 |
| Lean | always | the whole ghost tilts | toward clamp(vx/U·0.12, ±0.16) + clamp(dx/W·0.12, ±0.06) rad; spring k 60, damping 9 |
| Trail | moving | the lower body and hem lag behind | offset −vx/U·0.22 (±0.22), −vy/U·0.12 (±0.1), rate 6; weighted by smoothstep(−0.15, 0.5, y)² |
| Hem wave | always | four scallops travel along the hem | phase speed 2.4 + abs(vx)/U·3 rad/s; lobes s^0.7, notches −0.35·s^1.6, amplitude 0.065 |
| Gaze | always | both eyes slide toward the target | spring k 150, damping 17 toward the unit direction × min(1, distance / 1.2U) (vertical × 0.85); eye offset gx·0.075U, gy·0.06U |
| Look around | no cursor (before the first move, after it leaves the window, on window blur) | target circles the window | (CX + cos(0.4t)·0.3W, CY + sin(0.55t)·0.2H) |
| Hover | cursor inside the body's outline | eyes → ^ ^, body +4%, all glows up | happy rate 8 in / 5 out; glow rate 4; back glow α +0.12, pattern 3.5 → 5.5%, aura α +0.15 / +0.2, inner light α +0.2 |
| Click on it | pointer down while hovering | squash, > < eyes, sparkles, big ripple, hop | press = 1, fades 2.6/s (> < while > 0.4); squash velocity +7 (spring k 200, damping 8; ×(1 + 0.9sq) wide, ×(1 − 0.75sq) tall about the hem); hop +150 px/s; 26 sparkles at the cursor; ring 0.55U → 1.45U over 1.1 s |
| Click elsewhere | pointer down off the body | small ripple there, flinch, look | ring 0.06U → 0.56U over 1.1 s; surprise ≥ 0.45 (fades 1.3/s: brief dot eyes and a wider RGB split) |
| Startle | smoothed cursor speed > 1700 × U/340 px/s, not hovering, surprise < 0.6 | dot eyes, hop, glitch | surprise = 1; hop +200 px/s; 6 sparkles just above the centre; body alpha flickers 1 − 0.45·s·(0.5 + 0.5 sin 40t); RGB split = U·(0.018 + 0.05·s + 0.02·press) |
| Sleep | cursor present, not hovering, no move for > 5 s | eyes → sleepy, bob and hem slow to 40%, "z" | sleep rate 1.2 in (6 out); sleepy eyes once sleep > 0.5; a "z" with probability 0.7·dt per frame while sleep > 0.8 |
| "z" | while asleep | rises from the top right | from (x + 0.32U, y − 0.4U): up 0.35U, right 0.12U, wobble ±0.04U, size 0.07U → 0.12U, alpha sin(π·u)·0.8 over 2.4 s |
| Wake | the first move (or touch) while sleep > 0.5 | dot eyes, one hop | surprise ≥ 0.7; hop +240 px/s, **once per nap** |
| Hops | any hop | up and back down | gravity 1300 × U/340 px/s²; landing faster than 150 px/s adds squash min(6, 0.012·v); the floor glow fades with height |
| Blink | every 2.2–4.8 s (first at 2 s), only with plain eyes | eyes close and open | 0.16 s triangle; skipped while happy > 0.3, press > 0.1, surprise > 0.2 or sleep > 0.3 |
| Eye morph | any expression change | each eye's 72-point outline | each weight springs to its target: stiffness happy 170, press 420, surprise 220, sleep 60, blink 900, damping 0.92 × critical; blend priority press > happy > surprise > sleep > blink > open |
| Sparkles | click, startle | stars and dots fly out | speed (160–580)·U/340 px/s, −60 px/s upward kick, drag e^(−2.8t), gravity 40 px/s²; life 0.6–1.2 s; size (2–7)·U/340; 55% four-point stars that spin; colours cycle cyan, lilac, pink, white; alpha (1 − u)^1.4; additive with a 10 px glow |
| Dust | always | 26 motes | drift up 8·s px/s, sway ±6 px, twinkle 0.25–1 × 0.65 alpha; additive |
| Scanlines | always | thin bands drift down inside the body | step max(3, 0.012U), band 35% of the step, 7% alpha, 0.04U px/s |

**Touch (phones and tablets).** The finger is the cursor: a touch moves the cursor to the finger at once (no flick,
so a tap never startles it), a finger resting or sliding on the body is the hover (happy arches only while it's down),
a tap on the body is the click (hit-tested at the tap point itself), a tap elsewhere the flinch, a drag leads the eyes
and a quick swipe startles it. Lifting the finger leaves the cursor where it was: the ghost keeps looking there and
falls asleep after 5 s; the next touch wakes it with the same single hop. A touch's own `pointerleave` is ignored (only
a mouse leaving the window means "no cursor").

**Wake-up hop.** In the original concept every `pointermove` while asleep added another +240 px/s, so a normal wake
(several move events) launched the ghost off the top of the screen. Here the hop fires once per nap (`G.woke`).

**Reduced motion** (`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, read at start and on change): the startle doesn't flicker; the
body sits at its average alpha (1 − 0.225·surprise) instead. Everything else stays, since the piece is a direct
response to your own input.

